## Same-sample exact construction

[RUN] The modeled panel mirrors C1REALV2: world 1 steps 0–17 and world 2 steps
0–18, 37 anchors total, setting `a-r0`, carrier `nearest-eligible`, 100 users,
the shipped bounded catalogue, unchanged calibration, and boundary `(0,)`.
Per-anchor exact construction took mean `386.6643`, median `374.2304`, and range
`329.4410`–`535.7481` seconds per anchor, including exact source and catalogue
work and excluding the separately receipted per-process provider/tape setup.

[RUN] For every generation process, the imported pilot module's
`PILOT_PRIMITIVE_SOURCE_FALLBACK` began `True`, was set to `False` in-process
before `_build_anchor_rows`, and was restored to `True` in `finally`. The
bounded catalogue was then enumerated by `_catalogue_with_census`, and
`_exact_interactions` supplied exact normalized `joint`, `additive`, and `Psi`
values. Generation held and released one anchor's source/evaluator rows at a
time. The catalogue census reports zero candidate-shortlist misses and zero
shortlist-superset misses at every anchor.

[RUN] A C3-specific construction correction was necessary. The declared route
state is `_route_state(row, "C3") = (*row.q1_state, *row.q2_state)`, while the
pilot `_coalition_context` currently places Q1 alone in each member. The fitted
diagnostic contexts preserve that function's physical/resource fields but put
Q1+Q2 into both selected and incumbent member states. V2 repairs both Q1 parts
through `mcrl-v025-stagec-q1-action-v2` and leaves Q2 unchanged; v1 retains the
original Q1+Q2. This is why the observed member widths are 80 (v2) and 82 (v1),
and invariant-vector dimensions are 324 (v2) and 328 (v1).

[RUN] Production `CoalitionRow` deliberately rejects `|A| < 2`. To evaluate the
declared full support without inventing invalid production rows, compact
diagnostic records carry exact targets/sizes for all candidates, while complete
`CoalitionContext` vectors are constructed only for the 7,791 trainable rows.
This is a genuine C3 deviation from C1's per-action row construction. C3 also
uses direct scalar MSE rather than C1's pairwise/gauge objective; no C1 pair cap
or gauge was imported.

[RUN] Source generation used the sealed eight-action selection shortlist because
that is the support consumed by the bounded catalogue; it did not generate the
2,000 off-selection legal actions per anchor that the catalogue census records
as outside support. This avoids off-support exact work without omitting a
catalogue candidate: each anchor has zero selection-shortlist and superset
misses. This differs from the source-only research note's conservative
`full_legal_actions=True` suggestion, not from the fitted bounded support.

## Learner and metric protocol

[RUN] The sealed primary is the repository `AdamMLPHead`, evaluated with the
declared `AdamSetInteractionHead` hard-zero semantics: hidden `(64,64)`, ReLU,
learning rate `1.0e-3`, Adam betas `(0.9,0.999)`, epsilon `1e-8`, zero weight
decay, loss weight 1, 2,000 deterministic full-batch epochs, and no early
selection. The diagnostic creates the standalone C3 network directly from each
fold seed, matching C1REAL's diagnostic initialization convention; it does not
advance a production orchestrator RNG through C1 and C2 initializations.

[RUN] Level `R²` is pooled on raw held-out `Psi_A/kappa` values with no
test-time re-gauging. Pairwise ordering uses all non-tied true candidate pairs
within an anchor, truth ties within `1e-12` excluded and prediction ties within
`1e-15` worth 0.5. Top-1 uses stable predicted argmax and credits any true
maximum within `1e-12`. The sensitivity repeats all three after excluding
`|A| <= 1`.

## Permutation invariance

[RUN] The declared invariance passes empirically. For every trainable context, member order was
reversed before recomputing the declared invariant vector and the fitted head's
score. The pre-fit invariant-vector maximum difference was `2.2737e-13`. Across
sealed held-out scoring, the maximum score difference was `1.9895e-13` and
there were zero violations above `1e-12` (v1 maximum `1.8474e-13`, also zero
violations).

