A source audit caught one important implementation detail before execution: the engine’s `_objective` is only \(B-\eta E\); the prompt’s deployed score requires adding the exact κ-priced handover preference, equivalently subtracting positive `Phi_cost`. The runner now computes that full score exactly. I’m also seeding the sampled k=2–4 searches with the previously identified four-user RSS-relative catalogue move and its subsets, while rescoring it on EE rather than trusting its earlier F-based selection.
