I’m tightening the metric interpretation before launching: candidate `ΔF` will come from the mandated realised boundary-0 selector surface, while candidate `ΔEE` and service will come from the project’s realised full-48 endpoint surface. To keep that exact dual scoring tractable, the higher-k budget is 512 unique profiles per anchor/start/k (still seeded and mixed); k=1 remains exhaustive. The full-48 evaluator created for parity will be retained and reused for candidate endpoint batches, so there is only one fresh endpoint evaluator per anchor.
