## `eta_ref`, physical core, and full deployed `F`

- Exact calibration artifact: `eta_ref = 14235186615308645000000 / 1300834130903823 = 10943122.01465532 bit/J`; it is stored on the single JSON line in [PILOT_NOT_CLAIM-calibration.json](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/artifacts/v025-pilot-c3-20260909-PILOT_NOT_CLAIM/PILOT_NOT_CLAIM-calibration.json:1). PANELCEIL names that file and loads every price as `Fraction` ([PANELCEIL lines 27–34](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-ceiling30-ws/.scratch/panelceil/run_panelceil.py:27), [lines 133–145](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-ceiling30-ws/.scratch/panelceil/run_panelceil.py:133)). The origin routine sets it to realised full-grid BASE `bits/joules` at development step 0 ([pilot lines 274–296](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py:274)). The exact value is also persisted in the BASIN2 receipt ([lines 163643–163648](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-basin-ws/.scratch/basin2/basin2-receipt.json:163643)).
- Critical naming hazard: `runner._objective(profile, calibration)` delegates to `network_objective`, which is **only** `B - eta_ref E`; the source explicitly says Phi stays separate ([engine lines 1149–1155](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/probe/run_v025_matrix_probe.py:1149), [targets lines 130–145](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/physics_v025/targets.py:130)). BASIN2's earlier “exact F” tables therefore measure the physical core, not the brief's full `F = B - eta_ref E - Phi_cost`.
- `phi_qos` is a higher-is-better negative dimensionless preference: satellite change `-1`, same-satellite beam change `-0.5` ([targets lines 72–81](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/physics_v025/targets.py:72)); the constants are declared at [constants lines 70–71](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/physics_v025/constants_v025.py:70). The exact full raw-bit score is:

