## Minimal implementation recommendation

1. Copy only pure source/reconstruction ideas into a new local driver; import the read-only pilot/engine.
2. Install the class-wide raising stub before tape construction/evaluation, build only world 1, and assert the 12-anchor list explicitly.
3. Reconstruct RSS and crowded starts; endpoint-score BASE + both starts first and abort unless both pooled parity checks pass.
4. For each start/anchor, create exactly one fresh boundary-0 realised selection evaluator with BASE + start + initial candidates in its first batch. Generate candidates under a declared exhaustive/sampled budget, but select improvements using full-48 EE values from the one separate endpoint evaluator. Record boundary-0 full `ΔF`, full-48 `ΔEE`, and service for every candidate.
5. Reconstruct the deployed BASE-anchored catalogue by adapting BASIN2's dense-only bounded-catalogue block; exact-match every improving candidate's full assignments. Only after this identity check report the inside-support fraction and changed-set-size distribution.
6. End with assertions for 12/12 anchors, zero scalar calls, parity, full service classification, process/thread/niceness/RSS limits, and printed peak RSS.
